<!-- Exercise 027 - EmptyStateFallback (beginner).
     Goal:   Drive IsVisible on two sibling elements straight from a
             collection's Count, with no converter and no code-behind.
     Drills: IsVisible driven by an empty collection, via the ! / !!
             binding-path negation operators.
     Passes: dotnet test, filtered to Ex027_ (see the exact command in
     Ex027_EmptyStateFallback.axaml.cs - an XML comment may not hold two
     hyphens in a row, so it cannot appear here). -->
<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:b="clr-namespace:FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner"
             x:Class="FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner.Ex027_EmptyStateFallback"
             x:DataType="b:Ex027_EmptyStateFallbackViewModel">
  <!-- TODO: replace this placeholder with:
         <StackPanel Spacing="8">
           <TextBlock Name="EmptyMessage" Text="No items yet"
                      IsVisible="{CompiledBinding !Items.Count}" />
           <ItemsControl Name="ItemsPanel" ItemsSource="{CompiledBinding Items}"
                         IsVisible="{CompiledBinding !!Items.Count}">
             <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
               <DataTemplate x:DataType="x:String">
                 <TextBlock Text="{CompiledBinding}" />
               </DataTemplate>
             </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
           </ItemsControl>
         </StackPanel>
       Avalonia's binding path grammar coerces an int Count to bool and negates
       it: "!Items.Count" is true exactly when the collection is empty, and
       "!!Items.Count" double-negates back to true exactly when it is not. A
       ValueConverter would also work, but this negation idiom is the intended
       answer here - it needs nothing but the two bindings above. Hard-coding
       IsVisible="True"/"False" on either element matches only one state; the
       test drives the collection empty -> non-empty -> empty again and checks
       both elements flip in opposite directions every time. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock Text="TODO" />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
